    "\n",
    "**150 NL→SQL question pairs** across 5 complexity tiers (30 per tier), covering **all 15 Urban Observatory themes** (Air Quality, Traffic, Weather, Noise, Water Quality, Environment, Building, …). Questions are grounded in the full 2013-to-present population dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Tier | N | Complexity | SQL Patterns | Decision Level (Anthony, 1965) |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| T1 | 30 | Single-table lookup | SELECT, WHERE, DISTINCT, LIMIT, COUNT | Operational |\n",
    "| T2 | 30 | Single-table aggregation | GROUP BY, HAVING, aggregate functions, variance approx | Operational |\n",
    "| T3 | 30 | Two-table join | JOIN (exactly 2 tables), subquery in WHERE/HAVING | Managerial |\n",
    "| T4 | 30 | Window / 3-table join | RANK, ROW_NUMBER, LAG, LEAD, NTILE, PERCENT_RANK | Managerial |\n",
    "| T5 | 30 | Multi-CTE cross-theme | WITH … AS chains, cross-variable analysis | Strategic |\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Benchmark validity (Walpole et al., §9.3):** Ground-truth SQL is validated against the full population database. Because we use the complete archive ($N$ = all readings, not a sample), the ground-truth result sets represent true population outcomes — model accuracy proportions are then subject to Wilson CI inference (§19).\n"
