    "#### Decision rule\n",
    "\n",
    "Significance level $\\alpha = 0.05$ throughout. We follow the **P-value rule** (Walpole §10.3, p. 351; Lind Ch 10 Step 5): reject $H_0$ when $p < \\alpha$. All multi-comparison families are protected by Holm–Bonferroni and Benjamini–Hochberg FDR (see §19.1 below). Type I error ($\\alpha$) and Type II error ($\\beta$, hence power $1-\\beta$) are reported per test as required by Walpole §10.2 (p. 341).\n",
